---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Two Filters — baconpaul">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <a class="back" href="/sidequests/">← Sidequests</a>
    <div class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sidequest</p>
      <h1>Two Filters</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Two Filters, Two Step Sequencers, and some fixed mod paths.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="download">Download the <a href="https://github.com/baconpaul/two-filters/releases/tag/v1.0.0">v1.0.0 Stable Release</a></p>
      <p class="download">Download the <a href="https://github.com/baconpaul/two-filters/releases/tag/Nightly">Nightly Release</a></p>
      <p class="download">Access <a href="https://github.com/baconpaul/two-filters">the Source Code</a></p>
      <img src="/images/two-filters.png" alt="Two Filters screenshot" />
      <p>
        Two Filters is a stereo effect built around, well, two filters. It pairs a pair of
        configurable filters with a flexible modulation system so you can shape and
        sweep them in a variety of ways.
      </p>
      <p>
        Really, it's a test bed for our new Filter API. But you may find it fun. Some people have!
      </p>
      <p>
        The key features are
        <ul>
          <li>Two filters which can run in series or parallel, each with a wide range of filter types
          <li>A modulation system with a shapable step LFO and fixed mod paths 
          <li>A variety of routing and mixing options between the two filters
        </ul>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
